  </section>

  <!-- Glimpse 05: Himalayan Mountain Ecology & Civic Harmony -->
  <section class="space-y-8 scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-h)+4rem)]" id="mountain-ecology">
    <ChapterHeader
      chapter="Glimpse 05"
      title="Himalayan Ecology & Community Life in Sanjauli"
      tibetanTitle="ཁོར་ཡུག་གཅེས་སྐྱོང་དང་ས་གནས་མཐུན་ལམ།"
      lede="Rooted on the cedar slopes above Shimla, Main Jonang Takten Phuntsok Choeling thrives in mindful equilibrium with Himachal Pradesh's mountain ecology and surrounding community."
    />

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 space-y-4 font-serif text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display text-ink font-normal m-0">
          Ahimsa, Mountain Forest & Good Neighbors
        </h3>

        <p class="m-0">
          <strong>Ahimsa with Mountain Wildlife:</strong> Sanjauli and neighboring Jakhu hill are renowned for native troops of Rhesus macaque monkeys. For the monastery, monkeys are daily companions rather than adversaries. Monks carry wooden staffs (<em>'khar gsil</em>) across the courtyards—not to strike, but to tap the flagstones firmly to deter food-snatching, honoring Buddhist non-violence toward all mountain creatures.
        </p>

        <p class="m-0">
          <strong>Environmental Arboriculture:</strong> Recognizing the fragility of the Himalayan watershed, resident monks participate in annual tree-planting drives, reinforcing steep ravines with indigenous pines and deodars, and conducting regular weekend cleanups to keep the forest pristine.
        </p>

        <p class="m-0 text-muted">
          <strong>Bazaar Friendships & Local Amity:</strong> Monks in warm fleece jackets negotiate the Sanjauli market staircases alongside local Himachali, Pahari, and Punjabi merchants. During festivals like Tibetan Losar and Indian Diwali, gifts of deep-fried Tibetan pastries (<em>khapsey</em>) and festive Indian sweets (<em>mithai</em>) are warmly exchanged.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-6">
        <div class="surface-card overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border shadow-card">
          <Image
            src={plantingTreesImg}
            alt="Jonang monks participating in arboriculture and tree planting on the Himalayan ridges"
            class="w-full h-auto aspect-[4/3] object-cover transition-transform duration-700 hover:scale-105"
            width={640}
            height={480}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <div class="p-4 bg-surface-subtle border-t border-border">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-accent font-bold block mb-1">
              Active Arboriculture & Watershed Care
            </span>
            <p class="text-xs text-muted font-serif m-0">
              Preserving the deodar pine forests and slope stability of the Shimla hills through communal tree-planting.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Glimpse 06: Grounded Wisdom & Monastic Proverbs -->
  <section class="space-y-8 scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-h)+4rem)]" id="monastic-lore">
    <ChapterHeader
      chapter="Glimpse 06"
      title="Grounded Wisdom: Monastic Wit & Mountain Lore"
      tibetanTitle="དགོན་པའི་གཏམ་དཔེ་དང་བསླབ་བྱ།"
      lede="Himalayan monastic culture pairs profound meditative discipline with self-effacing humor, good-natured wit, and an intolerance for spiritual pretense."
    />

    <!-- Novice Writing & Mentorship Feature -->
    <div class="surface-card p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-border grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-center">
      <div class="md:col-span-5">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border">
          <Image
            src={youngStudentsImg}
            alt="Young novice monks studying classical Tibetan scripture together"
            class="w-full h-auto object-cover aspect-[4/3]"
